; Copy this file to `.npmrc` in the repository root:
;
;   cp .npmrc.example .npmrc
;
; `.npmrc` is ignored by git and must never be committed. This file, with the
; placeholder, is the one that is committed.
;
; The token is available at https://collaborators.vinovalab.ai, in the details
; of your challenge. It needs `read:packages`. Without it `npm install` fails
; with a 401, because @vinovalab/storage-connector-contract is published to
; GitHub Packages and not to the public registry.
;
; Either paste the token in place of the placeholder below, or leave the line as
; it is and export NODE_AUTH_TOKEN from your `.env`:
;
;   set -a; . ./.env; set +a
;
; Beware of the middle ground: if you leave `${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}` and never
; export it, npm does not complain. It sends the literal text to the registry
; and the 401 looks like a bad token instead of a missing variable.
;
; The same two lines work in ~/.npmrc if you would rather keep one copy for
; every repository.

@vinovalab:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
